{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775499886,"nonce":"WQwXtLaDNSJdSRlau85wHqOm+0o=","title":"Copy Claude Code plugins into container for skill availability","message":"Copy Claude Code plugins directory into container for skill availability\n\n## Context\nClaude Code plugins (like caveman — 75% token savings) are installed in ~/.claude/plugins/ on the host. The host directory is mounted at /claude-auth:ro, but docker-entrypoint.sh only copies credentials files (settings.json, .credentials.json). Claude Code inside the container can't find installed plugins.\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_entrypoint_codex_config.py::test_entrypoint_copies_plugins_dir\n  Assert: when /claude-auth/plugins/ exists, it is recursively copied to $HOME/.claude/plugins/\n- tests/test_entrypoint_codex_config.py::test_entrypoint_no_plugins_dir\n  Assert: when /claude-auth/plugins/ does not exist, no error occurs and $HOME/.claude/plugins/ is not created\n\n## Files\n- docker-entrypoint.sh (modify — add plugins copy block after existing credential copies)\n\n## Implementation\n1. After the existing credential copy block (line 8), add:\n```sh\n# Copy plugins so Claude Code can discover installed skills (e.g. caveman)\nif [ -d /claude-auth/plugins ]; then\n    cp -r /claude-auth/plugins \"$HOME/.claude/plugins\"\nfi\n```\n2. This goes inside the existing `if [ -d /claude-auth ]; then` block, after the three `cp` lines.\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee the existing credential copy pattern in docker-entrypoint.sh lines 4-9.\n\n## Notes\n- Plugins dir is ~38MB. One-time copy at startup, acceptable.\n- Read-only mount means we must copy, not symlink (Claude Code may need write access to plugin cache).\n- Only applies when agent_kind is claude-code (but the copy is harmless for other agents).\n\nREQ: REQ-001","files":null}]}